      "message": "[warning] Line 1196: 🟡 **Transport-CC feedback builder drops receive history on truncation.** `createRtcpTransportCcFeedback()` moves and clears all `receivedPackets` up-front, but caps the report to `MAX_TRANSPORT_CC_FEEDBACK_PACKETS` and `break`s when limit/gap is hit. Remaining packets are discarded instead of being sent in the next feedback packet, which can create artificial loss and destabilize bitrate control under bursty/high-rate traffic. **Fix:** keep unsent tail packets in state (or process in chunks) and only erase packets actually serialized into this RTCP feedback.",
